Building and Running
--------------------

You'll need to have applied all the patches in the 'patches/ee-gcc' project in
cvs to even think about building this example.  See the patches/README.

If you've done the above, 'make run' should build and run it.  As with all
ueber-Makefile projects, you can add a build name to the command line (debug,
optimized, and release by default).  'make debug' is useful when stepping
through in gdb.

See the usage printed on stdout when the program is run.

Files
-----

If you're looking for info about vectors, take a look at cloth.cpp.  Otherwise,
you'll find main() in cloth_app.cpp, which contains the main loop and code
specific to this application.  It defines CClothApp, a subclass of CPs2App which
contains code that can be reused across applications.

Try pressing the select button to switch between libvu0 vectors and ps2stuff
vector classes.. aside from being much more readable, they're twice as fast in
this example.  (In a more computation-intensive application the difference can
be even greater.)

